## 2026-11-19 -- US-001: Parse role strings

Created `src/config.ts` with:
- `ROLE_OPTIONS` -- shared option definitions for -m/--model,
  --effort, --max-turns, --prefer-subagent, used by both the
  role-string parser and the yargs run command in index.ts
- `parseRoleString(input)` -- parses a role string like
  "claude -m opus --effort high --max-turns 40 --prefer-subagent"
  into a ParsedRole object using yargs in non-CLI mode with
  strict validation

Refactored `src/index.ts` to import ROLE_OPTIONS from config.ts
instead of defining the four shared options inline. This satisfies
the "shared, not copied" requirement.

Added `src/config.ts` to the second esbuild call in build-esm.
Added `test/config.test.ts` with 11 pure tests to TESTS in
scripts/test.sh. Updated AGENTS.md project structure and module
boundaries to include config.

Gotchas:
- yargs strict mode rejects bare positionals; the parser uses a
  `$0 <provider>` command pattern so the provider is consumed as
  a named positional
- `--prefer-subagent` with no value gives `""` from yargs (type
  string); the parser coerces it to `"true"` to match the AC
- tapzero `t.throws` regex matches `caught.message`, not the
  full string; yargs error messages say "Unknown argument: X"
  without the `--` prefix
